Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:39:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: server item configs set stockmarket instead of tradeable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. `ItemServerCodec.createData` copies an item's server config entry over the cache data, but it assigns the
entry's `tradeable` to `stockmarket`:

    stockmarket = customData.tradeable

So `ItemServerType.tradeable` keeps its default `true` for every item, even where `items.toml` says
`tradeable = false` (coal bag, quest items, ...), and every item that has a config entry without a `tradeable`
line is put on the Grand Exchange (`stockmarket = true`), whatever the cache says. Code that asks "is this
tradeable" (for example `PlayerDeathDrops.isUntradeable`) gets the wrong answer.

Change. `tradeable = customData.tradeable`; `stockmarket` keeps the cache's value.

Tests. New `ItemServerCodecTest` (`:or-cache:test`): a config entry with `tradeable = false` makes the item
untradeable; an entry without it keeps a non-GE item off the GE and a GE item on it. The first two fail before
the change. Found while adding a looting bag (which must refuse untradeable items): on the server, the coal bag
and a quest key both reported `tradeable = true`.

Caveats. Behaviour changes for every item with a config entry: items the cache does not list on the Grand Exchange
stop counting as `stockmarket`, and items marked `tradeable = false` become untradeable for the code that checks
it (death drops, shops that check `tradeable || stockmarket`). That is the intended data, but worth a look at
anything that relied on the old values. The packed server cache must be rebuilt.

